-- title:
--   Full Slice Commutation Of Evaluated On Evaluated Questions
-- statement:
--   **Full-slice commutation obtained from evaluated-slice commutation.**
--
--   Let $S$ be a symmetric strategy on the $(m+1)$-dimensional space with normalized state $\psi$, and let $G^x$ be an indexed family of degree-$d$ polynomial projective measurements. Let $\gamma$ and $\zeta$ be the diagonal-commutativity and slice self-consistency errors. Assume $\gamma\ge0$, $\zeta\ge0$, the family is strongly self-consistent with error $\zeta$, and the evaluated full-slice product families satisfy the state-dependent squared operator-distance relation with error `commDataProcessedGError` at $(\gamma,\zeta)$. Let $\mathcal U$ be the uniform distribution on evaluated-slice questions, and let $P_L$ and $P_R$ be the ordered and reversed full-slice product families pulled back along the associated full-slice question map. Then
--
--   $$
--   \operatorname{SDDOpRel}_{\psi,\mathcal U}\left(P_L,P_R;30m\left(\gamma^{1/4}+\zeta^{1/4}+\left(\frac{d}{q}\right)^{1/4}\right)\right).
--   $$
--
--   This conclusion is exactly `comMainError` for the parameters $\gamma$ and $\zeta$. The lemma combines the two scalar marginalization estimates with the evaluated commutation estimate.
--
--   Formalization credit: Sirui Lu, Ruixuan Deng, Yanqiao Zhu, and Zhengfeng Ji (arXiv:2609.19814). Mathematical source: Zhengfeng Ji, Anand Natarajan, Thomas Vidick, John Wright, and Henry Yuen (arXiv:2009.12982).
--
--   **Formalization Note.** The source declaration is `MIPStarRE.LDT.Commutativity.fullSliceCommutation_of_evaluated_on_evaluated_questions`; its Lean statement gives the exact quantifier order and all boundary hypotheses.
-- source:
